 "answer": "The pgvector `<#>` operator returns the **negative inner product** of two vectors, as a `double precision` value.\n\nIt's negated so that `ORDER BY embedding <#> query` sorts nearest-first in ascending order, the same way distance operators do. To get the actual inner product, multiply the result by -1:\n\n```sql\nSELECT (embedding <#> '[1,2,3]') * -1 AS inner_product FROM items;\n```\n\nFor normalized vectors, the inner product equals cosine similarity.",
